    "description": "Hemingray Glass Company\nHemingray - 60 (CD 257) Cable Insulator\nCarnival Glass, Marigold Iridescent, Mid-Century\nThe Hemingray No. 60, classified by collectors as CD 257, is celebrated for its dual-eared crown, widely known as the \"Mickey Mouse\" insulator. Originally engineered for secondary power cables, examples finished in marigold carnival glass with vivid iridescent flash are prized for their striking industrial display appeal.\nSignature dual-eared saddle groove crown design\nMarigold carnival glass treatment featuring radiant rainbow iridescence\nEmbossed on lower skirt: \"HEMINGRAY - 60\" with date code on front, \"MADE IN U.S.A. 5\" on reverse\nMolded round drip points intact along the base perimeter\nMeasures approximately 5 x 5 inches\nCondition:\nIn very good vintage condition. Base drip points are intact with no major chips or missing points. Crown ears display smooth contours with minor mold line roughness and tiny fleabites typical of vintage utility glass. Luster and iridescence remain bright and vibrant throughout.\nThank you for all of your support!",
